    "story": "Serverless compute runs in the Databricks-managed serverless plane, outside the customer's network. A Private Network Gateway (PNG), created inside the workspace's Network Connectivity Configuration (NCC), injects a managed NIC into a /28 subnet of the customer's hub VNet, delegated to Microsoft.Databricks/workspaces. Serverless traffic leaves through that NIC as if it originated in the hub, so it follows the hub's routes: through the hub's VPN / ExpressRoute gateway to on-premises databases, servers and APIs, and on to anything transitively connected. The workspace's own VNet (classic compute and private endpoints) is peered to the hub and is not on the serverless path. Requires the Premium tier; PNG on Azure is in Public Preview.",
